      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "While often dismissed as exploitation, Frogs helped establish tropes that would appear in later environmental horror. <a href=\"/movie/571\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"571\">The Birds</a> (1963) may have pioneered animal attack films, but Frogs added explicit ecological themes that influenced everything from <a href=\"/movie/578\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"578\">Jaws</a> (1975) to modern eco-horror like <a href=\"/movie/123105\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"123105\">The Bay</a> (2012). The film's emphasis on wealthy polluters facing nature's wrath particularly resonates with contemporary environmental justice themes."
      }
